        "original_id": "b7219411-eaa7-59e2-8a71-4ef900be3b65",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Othonna, Othonna capensis, Stangeria eriopus\n- Places: Africa, southern Africa, South Africa, Australia\n- Families: sunflower family, Asteraceae, Stangeriaceae\n- Related genera: Bowenia\n\nFacts:\n- Othonna is a genus of African plants in the sunflower family.\n- Stangeria eriopus is a cycad endemic to southern Africa.\n- Stangeria eriopus is the only species in the genus Stangeria.\n- Stangeria eriopus is most closely related to the Australian genus Bowenia, and together they form the family Stangeriaceae.\n- Othonna capensis, also known as Little Pickles, is a species in the genus Othonna and the family Asteraceae.\n- Othonna capensis is native to South Africa.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
